.TH "daharness" "1" "" ""
.SH NAME
daharness \(em daharness security framework services (Brain, ZAP, MSF
MCP, API gateway)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]daharness\f[R] [\f[I]\-\-daemon\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the daharness service stack for authorized security research:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Brain sidecar\f[R] \(em Unix\-socket tool dispatch core; the socket
lives at \f[I]$BRAIN_SOCKET\f[R] (system profile:
\f[B]/run/daharness/brain.sock\f[R]).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]OWASP ZAP daemon\f[R] \(em API access list kept to loopback; the
browser proxy binds \f[I]$ZAP_PROXY_BIND\f[R] (default 0.0.0.0).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Metasploit RPC/MCP\f[R] \(em msfrpcd on \f[I]$MSF_RPC_PORT\f[R]
(default 55553).
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]API gateway\f[R] \(em FastAPI on port 5000 (host lane), exposing
\f[I]/tools/execute\f[R], \f[I]/tools/search\f[R], \f[I]/memory/*\f[R],
\f[I]/scratch/*\f[R] and the streamable\-HTTP MCP endpoint
\f[I]/mcp\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[B]Wordlist preflight\f[R] \(em wordlist tree sanity\-checked before
serving.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-daemon\f[R]
Services only, no interactive chat loop.
This is the form used by the \f[I]daharness.service\f[R] systemd unit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The systemd units load \f[B]/etc/daharness/daharness.env\f[R] via
\f[I]EnvironmentFile=\f[R] (system profile: WORKSPACE_ROOT,
BRAIN_SOCKET, GATEWAY_HOST, GATEWAY_PORT, GATEWAY_API_KEY); operator
shells use the tree\(aqs \f[I].env\f[R] (\f[I]bootstrap.py\f[R],
\f[I]api_gateway.py\f[R] and \f[I]tool_repl.py\f[R] load it with
\f[I]override=True\f[R]).
See \f[B]daharness.env(5)\f[R].
.PP
Privileged lanes (raw\-socket scanning, low\-port OOB) are not part of
this baseline; they degrade honestly and are documented in
\f[B]daharness\-safety(7)\f[R].
.SH FILES
\f[I]/run/daharness/brain.sock\f[R] \(em Brain UDS (system profile)
